General load rating of the T network - nec/rating.py (design log §1.7, §1.7.1, §5, §6, §8D)

Loads are R + jX at the balanced output terminals. 'Key-down' applies every limit, including the RF
bay's 200 W (roller loss at Q 150 plus the input choke); 'PEP' drops only the 200 W budget. A band's
figure is the worst of its two edges and its center (kBands, fw/core/src/freq.cpp).
Limits: C1 9 kV pk, C2 6 kV pk, roller 18.4 A RMS and 9.3 kV pk, output 10 kV pk; ranges C2 20-675 pF,
roller 0.20-32.4 uH, C1 per part below.
Codes: VC1 = C1 voltage; VC2 = C2 voltage; IL = roller current; VL = roller voltage; Vout = output
voltage; heat-L = 200 W budget, mostly roller loss; heat-ch = 200 W budget, mostly choke heat; C1min = C1
minimum; C1max = C1 maximum; C2min = C2 minimum; C2max = C2 maximum; Lmin = roller minimum; Lmax = roller
maximum; ranges = C and L ranges together.
Self-check: vectorized choke heat against choke_screen.choke_loss, worst relative difference 9e-15.

